PROJECT NAME: IMovies — Online Movie Ticket Booking System

ROLE:
Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, system architect, UI/UX designer,
database engineer, and QA tester.

Your task is to design, develop, test, and document a complete, functional,
full-stack movie ticket booking web application called IMovies.

Do not create only a static UI or a frontend prototype. Build a working
application with a connected backend, persistent MongoDB database,
authentication, booking management, and real-time seat availability updates.

====================================================
1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
====================================================

IMovies is an online movie ticket booking platform that allows users to:

- Discover currently running movies and upcoming releases.
- Browse movie information, genres, languages, and ratings.
- Select a cinema, date, and showtime.
- View a visual seating layout.
- Select available seats.
- See the total ticket price before confirming a booking.
- Reserve seats and receive a booking confirmation.
- View their booking history.
- Cancel eligible bookings according to the cancellation policy.
- Manage their account and profile.

The application must provide a seamless, responsive, and secure movie-booking
experience across desktop computers, tablets, and mobile devices.

The platform must have two main user roles:

1. Customer
2. Administrator

Customers can browse movies and book tickets.

Administrators can manage movies, theatres, screens, showtimes, pricing,
bookings, and users through a protected administration dashboard.

