7. SEAT SELECTION AND AVAILABILITY
====================================================

Create a visual cinema seating layout.

Requirements:

- Display a screen indicator at the top.
- Organize seats into rows and columns.
- Assign each seat a unique identifier, such as A1, A2, B1, and B2.
- Distinguish available seats from selected seats.
- Distinguish booked seats from temporarily reserved seats.
- Display a legend explaining seat statuses.
- Allow users to select multiple seats.
- Prevent selection of unavailable seats.
- Show selected seat identifiers.
- Calculate the total price dynamically.
- Display the number of selected seats.

Implement server-side protection against double booking.

IMPORTANT CONCURRENCY REQUIREMENT:

Two customers must not be able to successfully book the same seat for
the same showtime.

Do not rely only on frontend seat availability.

Use MongoDB transactions where supported by the deployment environment,
with appropriate unique database constraints and atomic reservation logic.

Create a reliable reservation mechanism with expiration for temporarily
held seats.

If using temporary reservations:
- Assign a reservation expiration time.
- Release expired reservations.
- Recheck seat availability during final booking confirmation.
- Prevent expired reservations from being confirmed.

If transactions are unavailable, implement an appropriate atomic reservation
strategy and document the limitations.

Use Socket.IO if practical to notify connected clients when seat availability
changes. The application must still work correctly without WebSockets.

